I found another problem related to the compilation, that said, I will increase it in the form of a comment:

Project demo link: https://stackblitz.com/edit/node-jacfrp

How to check (in stackblitz):
1. cd angular-tour-of-heroes
2. npm install
3. npm run start (or ng serve)

The code:
```
@import './design/abstracts/mixins';
@import './design/abstracts/variable';
@import './design/abstracts/maps';
@import './design/base/theme-bg';

::ng-deep {
  body {
    background: red;
  }
}
```

It is important to note that this time all comments have been removed for testing purposes.

If the following line: `@import './design/base/theme-bg';` is commented, the problem is solved.

That said, I believe there is also a problem when parsing the SCSS.

### The problem:
![image](https://github.com/angular/angular/assets/40347728/5bc2d4e7-bb33-4028-85d0-408716c607d7)

The error is that this red background code is actually in the **app.component.scss** file, **theme-bg** is just an import

The removal of CSS comments, also breaks all component styles sourcemaps when using the Angular CLI experimental esbuilder. This is because esbuild adds a comment at the top of the CSS like such;

```css
/* src/app/app.component.scss */
* {
   color: red;
}
/*# sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;base64,ewogICJ2ZXJzaW9uIjogMywKICAic291cmNlcyI6IFsic3JjL2FwcC9hcHAuY29tcG9uZW50LnNjc3MiXSwKICAic291cmNlc0NvbnRlbnQiOiBbIioge1xuICBjb2xvcjogcmVkO1xufVxuIl0sCiAgIm1hcHBpbmdzIjogIjtBQUFBO0FBQ0U7OyIsCiAgIm5hbWVzIjogW10KfQo= */
```

The compiler removes this comment which causes the sourcemap lines to shift.

issue.body:
Prior to this commit, comments in CSS were being removed. This caused inline sourcemaps to break to the shift in lines.

This caused sourcemaps to break in the ESBuild based builder as this always adds comments at the top of the file with the filename.

Example
```css
 /* src/app/app.component.scss */
* {
  color: red;
  background: transparent;
}
/*# sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;charset=utf-8;base64, */
```

Closes #50308
